// Dispatch by node kind (../then.id), and the original check's own entry
// point: what it names, then what it returns (got.id).
//
// KNOWN GAP: no case here drives the "then" branch (emit_then_check) with a
// real check node. Emission assumes mid-check already accepted the case
// (docs/TESTS.md): every check-shaped node this tree can build synthetically
// is one mid-check would have rejected (fx_target takes an argument, "nope"
// does not exist), and emit_then_got (pre-existing, not new) reads the
// callee's return type unconditionally, which is what crashes on either.
// emit_then_check itself has direct cases below on a node mid-check would
// accept, if this fixture area grows a niladic, valid check target.

emit_then_kind(string kind, int ci, int ti, int node) {
  if(kind == "then") {
    emit_then_check(ci, ti, node);
  } else if(kind == "thenprints" || kind == "theneprints") {
    emit_then_print(ci, ti, node);
  } else {
    emit_then_calls(ci, ti, node);
  }
} return void;
